For each pair of indices `(i, j)`, if `a[i]` is equal to `b[j]`, then `a[i]` is part of the LCS of `a[i:]` and `b[j:]`, so `dp[i][j]` is `a[i] + dp[i+1][j+1]`. Otherwise, `dp[i][j]` is the LCS of `a[i:]` and `b[j:]` that is either `dp[i+1][j]`, `dp[i][j+1]`, or `dp[i+1][j+1]`, whichever has the shortest length.

Finally, `dp[0][0]` is the LCS of `a` and `b`, and is returned.

